  ('lake-atitlan-guatemala', '10S', 'Lake Atitlán', 'Guatemala', '*If it''s the first pale light on three volcanoes', 'live', 'verified', 'desertDunes', 'Guatemala', '{"adventure","culture","expedition","romance","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Volcanic caldera lake at 1,562 m (5,125 ft), up to 340 m deep, ~130 km², ringed by three volcanoes — San Pedro, Tolimán, Atitlán (Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Atitlán, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Villages divide by role: Panajachel gateway hub, San Pedro backpacker/Spanish-school, San Marcos yoga/wellness, Santiago Atitlán largest/traditional, San Juan weaving + coffee (Source: adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Indian Nose sunrise hike (~30 min pre-dawn) is the signature caldera overlook; San Marcos offers yoga retreats + Cerro Tzankujil cliff-jump (Source: adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Dry season Nov–Apr is most photogenic; Christmas + Semana Santa fill weeks ahead; Sept–Oct rates 40–50% below peak (Source: atitlan.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Air access via GUA (La Aurora Intl) + shuttle/private transfer ~3 hr to Panajachel; boat (lancha) is the only road between villages (Source: theabroadblog.com / adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)"],"safety":{"emergency":"110 police · 122/123 ambulance · 1500 ASISTUR/PROATUR (or +502-2290-2810) — verify locally","hospital":"Panajachel/Sololá clinics + regional hospital for stabilization; serious trauma/cardiac evac to Guatemala City (~3 hr road); highlands lack tertiary trauma capability","l3_disclosure":true,"stay_in_zone":true,"founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on TWW''s BOOK WITH WARNING (Four-Bin v3) framing (same founder/attorney axis as the held Central-Mexico SR6)","air_access_verified":"GUA (La Aurora Intl) + shuttle/private transfer ~3 hr to Panajachel","altitude":"~1,562 m (5,125 ft) lakeside — mild; volcano summits San Pedro ~3,020 m / Atitlán ~3,535 m reach real altitude","malaria":"none — CDC reports no malaria transmission at Lake Atitlán (highland); insect-bite precautions only; dengue/Zika possible in Guatemala generally","water":"bottled/purified only","lake_boat_safety":"Xocomil wind kicks up late morning/afternoon and can capsize boats — cross early, licensed lanchas with life vests","swim_advisory":"verify current cyanobacteria (Microcystis) advisory before selling lake-swim (blooms 2009, 2015)","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guatemala","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:35Z","page_updated":"2026-08-13T14:45:16+01:00","source_country":"guatemala","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"Within 5km of the Mexican border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The towns of Santa Ana Huista, San Antonio Huista and La Democracia, in Huehuetenango","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"}]},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"Dry-season demand builds from late Sept / early Oct for the Nov–Apr window; retreat + honeymoon bookings run longer lead","peak":"Dry season Nov–Apr; sharpest spikes Christmas–New Year and Semana Santa; weekly Chichi-market micro-peak Thu/Sun","fire_date":"Mid-September for the Christmas/New-Year + Jan–Mar dry-season peak; early-to-mid January for the Semana Santa spike — curve-start minus 1–2 weeks (directional, sharpen on live tracking)","shoulder":"May–June and September–October","green":"May–October wet season — afternoon storms, greenest landscape, Sept–Oct rates 40–50% below peak","booking_lead":"Peak boutiques/villas 2–4 mo (longer for Christmas + Semana Santa); yoga retreats 2–6 mo; day tours day-of to 1 wk","off_season_specials":"Rainy-season wellness-retreat + language-immersion + villa packages; midweek boutique value; Chichi day-trip add-ons year-roun