oll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}],"dive_emergency_numbers_verified":{"read":"2026-08-30","numbers":{"+1-919-684-9111":"DAN 24/7 emergency hotline — dan.org/about-dan/contact/, read 2026-08-30"},"_rule":"Each number above was read from the authority named beside it on the date shown. ⛔ A number with no entry here has NOT been verified and must not be presented as an emergency contact."}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Mar (El Norte kite/wind season) - highest occupancy, schools full, villas booked; whale + whale-shark window","shoulder":"Apr & Oct (wind tapering / fishing ramping; softer rates)","green":"May-early Nov (glass-calm offshore = billfish/dorado peak + summer tournaments; desert heat + hurricane window Jun-Nov)","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"Apr-May/Oct = calm-water Sea of Cortez beach town + snorkel/SUP + ATV + Cabo Pulmo day trips; La Paz whale-shark add-ons Oct-Apr; summer = glass-calm offshore fishing + tournament energy","event_peaks":["El Norte kite/wind Nov-Mar","Dorado Shoot Out ~mid-July + East Cape Offshore / Bisbee''s opener","whale season Dec-Apr","La Paz whale sharks ~Oct-Apr"],"sources":["https://www.wahoowind.com/about","https://vanwormerresorts.com/sport-fishing","https://discoverbaja.com/2026/06/03/summer-2026-baja-fishing-tournaments/","https://sallysees.com/whale-watching-in-baja-california-sur/"],"fire_date":"open kite/wind campaigns late summer (for Nov-Mar); open sportfishing/tournament campaigns late winter (for May-Nov); market kite and fishing audiences separately - opposite seasons","booking_lead":"villas + fishing lodges for Nov-Mar wind season and summer tournament dates book 4-9 months ahead; tournament weeks (Dorado Shoot Out mid-July, East Cape Offshore) tightest; shoulder short-lead; verify current tournament dates"},"jewels":[{"name":"El Norte kiteboarding season (Nov-Mar)","status":"future","tier":"premier","bookable":"Wahoo Wind Co. / Vela Baja lessons + rentals","source":"https://www.wahoowind.com/about","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"reliable 15–30 kt N/NE cross-wind on a protected sandy bay","si":"ocean","blurb":"reliable 15–30 kt N/NE cross-wind on a protected sandy bay","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"kite-school operator on application + GYG affiliate","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","ocean":"primary","tropical":"destination"},"commi