e":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"gray-whale HARD window ~mid-Jan-mid-Mar (calving lagoon)","second_peak":"sardine run / striped-marlin bait ball, mid-Oct-Dec","shoulder":"late Dec-early Jan (arrival), late Mar-Apr (tail-end)","green":"May-Sep (off-season, hot, hurricane-exposed)","out_of_season_fill":"minimal; sport fishing + birding fill edges","fire_date":"gray-whale 9-12 months out; marlin/sardine-run by mid-summer for Oct-Dec","event_peaks":["US/Canada winter escape overlaps gray-whale peak"],"booking_lead":"6-12 months (tiny whale-camp capacity, both windows sell out early)"},"jewels":[{"status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Gray-whale calving-lagoon encounter","si":"expedition","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator; net-rate red","name":"Barrier-island whale-camp overnight","si":"expedition","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"status":"live","tier":"essential","commission":"operator","name":"Mangrove / birding skiff","si":"expedition","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"status":"future","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Snorkel-with-striped-marlin bait ball (sardine run)","si":"ocean","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","ocean":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"status":"future","tier":"luxury","commission":"operator/wholesale","name":"Striped-marlin liveaboard (Nautilus)","si":"ocean","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","ocean":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is gray-whale season in Magdalena Bay?","a":"The hard window is roughly mid-January to mid-March, when mothers and calves fill the calving lagoon; whales arrive late Dec–early Jan and linger to April. Mag Bay''s grays are famously \"friendly,\" often approaching the pangas — book the tiny whale-camp capacity 6–12 months ahead.","source":"seakayakadventures.com / randomtrip.net, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"Can I snorkel the striped-marlin bait balls?","a":"Yes, from about mid-October to December — but it''s an advanced open-water activity. You''re offshore in current among fast-moving marlin and sea lions driving sardines to the surface, so it''s for confident, fit snorkelers and freedivers with specialist operators only.","source":"magdalenabaywhales.com / divernet.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"Where do I stay — are there resorts?","a":"No resorts — the accurate options are a barrier-island whale camp (glamping, 1–7 nights, ~$650+ for a 1-night all-in) or basic hotels in Puerto San Carlos and López Mateos. The camp is part of the experience: whales from shore, and nothing between you and the lagoon.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"Is the bait-ball snorkel dangerous?","a":"It is not a beginner activity. The sardine run happens offshore in current among fast predators, so go only with specialist operators, follow the guide''s positioning rules and never touch the wildlife; if you dive elsewhere in Baja, the nearest chambers are La Paz and Cabo San Lucas with 18–24 h no-fly.","source":"divernet.com / sssnetwork.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Magdalena Bay — Gray-Whale Lagoon & Striped-Marlin Sardine Run | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Magdalena Bay, Baja California Sur: gray-whale calving lagoon (Jan-Mar) and the striped-marlin bait-ball sardine run (Oct-Dec). Whale-camp stays, seasons, safe-panga guidance.","long_tail":["gray whale season Magdalena Bay 2026","snorkel with striped marlin Baja","Magdalena Bay whale camp","Puerto San Carlos whale watching","how to get to Magdalena Bay from Los Cabos"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["ballena gris Bahia Magdalena","avistamiento de ballenas Puerto San Carlos","marlin rayado Bahia Magdalena","corrida de la sardina Baja","campamento de ballenas Bahia Magdalena"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristAttraction","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-04","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]},"primary_keyword":["Magdalena Bay whale watching","gray whale Magdalena Bay","striped marlin bait ball","Baja sardine run"]},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","ocean"],"ultra":[{"what":"National Geographic / Lindblad expedition cruise to Magdalena Bay (sea-based); or Los Cabos/East Cape ultra property as pre/post base","why_ultra":"small-ship expedition w/ naturalists is the only refined product on the bay; no land ultra exists here (nearest = Los Cabos/East Cape 3.5-6 h away)","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso; expedition-cruise lines carry advisor commission","virtuoso_value_add":"shipboard credit/expedition perks via preferred programs, or resort credit at Los Cabos base","mor":"resale via host-Virtuoso / cruise-wholesale only; Magdalena Bay lodging itself is NOT ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Magdalena Bay, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":24.6167,"lng":-112.1},"orbit":[{"id":"balandra-beach-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["tropical","family","romance"]},{"id":"cabo-pulmo-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["expedition","diveglobal"]},{"id":"cabo-san-lucas-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["liveaboard","expedition","ocean","ultra"]},{"id":"east-cape-mexico","jewels":7,"si":["romance","expedition","diveglobal","ocean"]},{"id":"espiritu-santo-island-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["expedition","ocean"]},{"id":"la-paz-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","tropical","diveglobal"]},{"id":"loreto-mexico","jewels":7,"si":["expedition","tropical","diveglobal","romance"]},{"id":"los-barriles-mexico","jewels":8,"si":["ocean","expedition","tropical"]},{"id":"san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["romance","expedition","culture","ocean"]},{"id":"todos-santos-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","culture","wellness","ocean"]}],"orbit_country":["akumal-mexico","bacalar-mexico","calakmul-mexico","campeche-city-mexico","cancun-mexico","careyes-mexico","celestun-mexico","chapala-ajijic-mexico","chichen-itza-mexico","coba-mexico","costalegre-mexico","cozumel-mexico","ensenada-mexico","guadalajara-mexico","guanajuato-city-mexico","holbox-mexico","huatulco-mexico","isla-contoy-mexico","isla-mujeres-mexico","izamal-mexico","mahahual-mexico","mazamitla-mexico","merida-mexico","mexico-city-mexico","oaxaca-city-mexico","palenque-mexico","playa-del-carmen-mexico","puerto-aventuras-mexico","puerto-morelos-mexico","puerto-vallarta-mexico","punta-mita-mexico","rio-lagartos-mexico","san-cristobal-de-las-casas-mexico","san-miguel-de-allende-mexico","san-sebastian-del-oeste-mexico","sayulita-mexico","sian-kaan-mexico","teotihuacan-mexico","tlaquepaque-mexico","tulum-mexico","uxmal-mexico","valladolid-mexico","valle-de-guadalupe-mexico","puerto-escondido-mexico"]}'::jsonb, 62),
