est river archipelago on Earth: 400 forested islands over 90 km of the Rio Negro, a UNESCO-caliber protected area of igarapés, black-water channels","si":"wildlife","blurb":"the second-largest river archipelago on Earth: 400 forested islands over 90 km of the Rio Negro, a UNESCO-caliber protected area of igarapés, black-water channels","commission":"DMC / lodge / riverboat; park fee non-commissionable","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","river":"destination","romance":"destination","wildlife":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Pink river dolphins (boto), Novo Airão","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.aventuradobrasil.com/blog/swimming-with-pink-dolphins-in-brazil/","hook":"the famous Rio Negro boto, encountered at regulated floating platforms ~180 km from Manaus; a genuine wildlife highlight","si":"wildlife","blurb":"the famous Rio Negro boto, encountered at regulated floating platforms ~180 km from Manaus; a genuine wildlife highlight","commission":"DMC day-trip / lodge excursion; platform-regulated","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","river":"destination","romance":"destination","wildlife":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Indigenous / ribeirinho community visit","tier":"comfort","source":"https://amazontourmanaus.com/manaus-amazon/the-amazon-rainforest/anavilhanas-national-park/item162","hook":"a visit to a river-people or indigenous community, done through a genuinely vetted, community-consenting operator","si":"wildlife","blurb":"a visit to a river-people or indigenous community, done through a genuinely vetted, community-consenting operator","commission":"vetted DMC / operator AOR only (ethical, community-consenting)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","river":"destination","romance":"destination","wildlife":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Teatro Amazonas opera house","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Theatre","hook":"the 1896 belle-époque jewel of the rubber boom: Alsatian roof tiles, Glaswegian steel, Carrara-marble stairs, a dome of 36,000 tiles in the national colours","si":"romance","blurb":"the 1896 belle-époque jewel of the rubber boom: Alsatian roof tiles, Glaswegian steel, Carrara-marble stairs, a dome of 36,000 tiles in the national colours","commission":"DMC / city-tour affiliate; performance/visit ticket non-commissionable","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["culture","romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"evidenced","river":"destination","romance":"primary","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"Romance & Honeymoons / Culture","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Romance & Honeymoons / Culture'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"},{"name":"Design jungle-lodge honeymoon (Mirante do Gavião / Anavilhanas)","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.here-away.com/mirantedogaviaoamazonlodge","hook":"a boutique design lodge over black water: canopy hammock, private dawn canoe, floating bar, spa/wellness space, dolphin-swim afternoon. The adventurous honeymoon","si":"romance","blurb":"a boutique design lodge over black water: canopy hammock, private dawn canoe, floating bar, spa/wellness space, dolphin-swim afternoon. The adventurous honeymoon","commission":"DMC lodge package / consortia (AOR)","wells":["stay","activities","shop"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","romance","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"evidenced","river":"destination","romance":"primary","ultra":"evidenced","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","package","consortia","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_basis":"tier==''ultra'' implies the ultra interest; gen_ultra_from_tier"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit Manaus & the Brazilian Amazon?","a":"**There are two completely different Amazons, and the water level decides which one you get.** High-water season (roughly March–August, peaking **June–July**) floods the forest — you *canoe through the trees*, boats glide deep into the *igapó*, wildlife moves along the flooded canopy. Low-water season (September–February) drops the river, exposes white-sand river beaches, opens longer forest trails, and concentrates fish and wildlife around shrinking channels — the season for hiking and fishing. Same place, two different trips.","source":"https://www.greenseashells.com/post/high-water-vs-low-water-in-the-brazilian-amazon-what-actually-changes-for-travelers","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"What is worth doing in Manaus & the Brazilian Amazon?","a":"**Meeting of the Waters (Encontro das Águas)** — the 6-km line where the warm dark Rio Negro and the pale cooler Solimões run side by side without mixing, the signature Amazon spectacle — **PRICE TIER `[essential]`** — COMMISSION: DMC / tour affiliate half-day; park fee non-commissionable","source":"https://www.viator.com/Manaus-attractions/Meeting-of-Waters/d4441-a6911"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Manaus & the Brazilian Amazon Travel Guide 2026 — Meeting of the Waters, Jungle Lodges & Amazon Cruises | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"pt-BR","local_keywords":["Manaus Amazônia o que fazer","Encontro das Águas passeio","cruzeiro Rio Negro Amazonas","melhores lodges de selva na Amazônia","botos cor-de-rosa Novo Airão","cachoeiras Presidente Figueiredo","Teatro Amazonas visita","vacina febre amarela Manaus","Manaus é seguro para turistas","lua de mel na Amazônia","arquipélago de Anavilhanas","Amazônia cheia e vazante melhor época"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brazil","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:23Z","source_updated":"2026-05-11T12:32:48+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Mirante do Gavião Amazon Lodge","lane":"Fora/consortia","mor":"consortia","tier":"ultra","note":"12-suite design lodge, Novo Airão / Anavilhanas edge"},{"name":"Anavilhanas Jungle Lodge","lane":"consortia/Fora","mor":"consortia","tier":"premier","note":"glass-wall bungalows, floating bar, pool, spa"},{"name":"Juma Amazon Lodge","lane":"consortia/DMC","mor":"consortia/DMC","tier":"comfort","note":"stilted treetop bungalows ~15m, solar-powered"},{"name":"Iberostar Grand Amazon (riverboat)","lane":"consortia/cruise affiliate","mor":"consortia/operator","tier":"premier","note":"72-cabin all-inclusive expedition; verify consortia lane"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Manaus & the Brazilian Amazon, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-3.119,"lng":-60.0217},"orbit":[{"id":"bonito-brazil","jewels":9,"si":["wildlife"]},{"id":"foz-do-iguacu-brazil","jewels":9,"si":["expedition","culture","romance"]},{"id":"pantanal-brazil","jewels":12,"si":["safari","wildlife","expedition"]}],"orbit_country":["fernando-de-noronha-brazil","jericoacoara-brazil","ouro-preto-tiradentes-brazil","rio-de-janeiro-brazil","sao-paulo-brazil","salvador-brazil"]}'::jsonb, 64),
  ('manuel-antonio-costa-rica', '10S', 'Manuel Antonio', 'Costa Rica', 'Sloths, monkeys and Pacific cliffs', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Costa Rica', '{"tropical","expedition","wildlife"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Manuel Antonio NP is open Wed–Mon 07:00–16:00, CLOSED every Tuesday; adult entry US$18, child (2–12) US$5, under-2 free; advance online ticket + passport number required.","One of few places to see all of Costa Rica''s iconic wildlife at a beach: 2- & 3-toed sloths, white-faced capuchins (90%+ of visits), endangered Central American squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans.","Two park beaches: crescent Playa Manuel Antonio (calm, turquoise — the calmest, patrolled swim) and longer, choppier Playa Espadilla Sur.","Access: ~2.5–3 hr / ~168 km drive from San José (SJO), OR ~25-min domestic flight to Quepos–Manuel Antonio (XQP) on Sansa / Costa Rica Green Airways + 15 km / 25-min transfer.","Cliffside-resort belt (Arenas del Mar, Makanda, Gaia, Tulemar) makes it a top romance/honeymoon hub; hillside villas make it a strong family/multi-gen hub."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Hospital Metropolitano Quepos (private, 24-hr, marina) + public Max Terán Valls Hospital; serious cases to San José major hospitals (~2.5–3 hr) with air evac available","l2_disclosure":true,"advisory_note":"standard caution — petty crime, don''t display wealth, avoid poorly lit beaches at night, enroll in STEP","air_access_verified":"SJO gateway; XQP (Quepos–Manuel Antonio) ~25-min domestic flight on Sansa / Costa Rica Green Airways, or ~2.5–3 hr drive from SJO","riptide":"HARD FLAG — rip currents are the leading cause of tourist drowning in Costa Rica (>80% of drownings); most beaches unguarded. Swim only at guarded/flagged beaches (the park cove is the calmest and patrolled), heed red flags, never swim alone; if caught, swim parallel to shore.","wildlife":"Bold habituated monkeys/raccoons/coatis raid food — no feeding, seal food, don''t leave bags unattended","dengue":"Year-round mosquito-borne risk (higher green season May–Nov); no widely available traveler vaccine — DEET/picaridin, cover at dawn/dusk, screened/AC rooms","water":"Tap water in San José & major tourist areas (incl. Manuel Antonio/Quepos) treated and generally safe; sensitive stomachs / remote lodges use bottled/filtered","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-09-01T16:20:27Z","page_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00","source_country":"costa-rica","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"late October–early November","peak":"mid-December–April (Christmas/New Year & Semana Santa ~1 yr lead)","fire_date":"2026-10-17","shoulder":"May–November (green-season value)","green":"May–November (afternoon rain; lush, lower rates)","booking_lead":"3–8 weeks normal peak; ~1 year for Christmas/New Year & Semana Santa (lead pressure on cliffside-resort + villa beds)","off_season_specials":"green-season resort/villa discounts + whale-watching backfill (Jul–Oct/Nov Southern-Hemisphere humpbacks)","event_peaks":["Whale season Jul–Oct/Nov (peak Aug–Sep)","Whale season Dec–Mar/Apr (peak Jan–Feb)","Christmas/New Year","Semana Santa (Easter)"],"operational_note":"Manuel Antonio NP closed every Tuesday — route park visit Wed–Mon; slot waterfalls/catamaran/mangrove on Tuesday"},"jewels":[{"name":"Playa Manuel Antonio (in-park)","status":"live","hook":"Crescent white sand + calm turquoise — the park''s calmest, patrolled swim and best snorkel, backed by monkey-filled rainforest.","bookable_category":"guided park tour / DIY ticket","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mustseespots.com/costa-rica/articles/manuel-antonio-national-park-beaches-wildlife-trails-explained/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April",