, meals, seasonal dolphins/whales — the signature on-the-water romance experience.","bookable_category":"catamaran tour / private charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/manuel-antonio/Snorkeling_Tours.php + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~4-hr coastal catamaran with snorkeling, meals, seasonal dolphins/whales — the signature on-the-water romance experience.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; DMC/host-IATA for private charter","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition","wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Nauyaca Waterfalls day trip","status":"live","hook":"~1.5 hr away; steep hike (or 4x4/horseback) to two massive cascades + natural swimming pools.","bookable_category":"guided day tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/things-to-do-in-manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~1.5 hr away; steep hike (or 4x4/horseback) to two massive cascades + natural swimming pools.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; host-IATA land services","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Damas Island mangrove kayak","status":"live","hook":"Calm-water estuary/mangrove kayak north of Quepos — monkeys, crocodiles and birds; superb family + wildlife half-day.","bookable_category":"half-day kayak tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/manuel-antonio/tours/Half-Day-Kayak-Damas-Mangroves.php + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"Calm-water estuary/mangrove kayak north of Quepos — monkeys, crocodiles and birds; superb family + wildlife half-day.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate + local operator; host-IATA private","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition","tropical","wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"evidenced","wildlife":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Rainmaker canopy + hanging bridges","status":"live","hook":"~1,400-acre private rainforest reserve with waterfalls, trails and Mistico-style suspension bridges — lower-crowd canopy near Manuel Antonio.","bookable_category":"guided canopy/bridges tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/things-to-do-in-manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","blurb":"~1,400-acre private rainforest reserve with waterfalls, trails and Mistico-style suspension bridges — lower-crowd canopy near Manuel Antonio.","when":"year-round","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; host-IATA land services","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Quepos marina sportfishing","status":"live","hook":"Marina Pez Vela — top Pacific billfish/sailfish + dorado sportfishing base; premier half/full-day charters.","bookable_category":"charter","tier":"premier","source":"https://costaricaexperts.com/destinations/manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Marina Pez Vela — top Pacific billfish/sailfish + dorado sportfishing base; premier half/full-day charters.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"host-IATA / private-charter agent-of-record; premium day rates","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Whale-watching (Marino Ballena / Uvita)","status":"live","hook":"~45–60 min south; two humpback seasons (Jul–Oct/Nov + Dec–Mar/Apr) at the whale''s-tail sandbar — spans both green & dry season.","bookable_category":"guided whale-watching boat tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://puravidamoms.com/whale-watching-uvita-tour-guide/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~45–60 min south; two humpback seasons (Jul–Oct/Nov + Dec–Mar/Apr) at the whale''s-tail sandbar — spans both green & dry season.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate + host-IATA; Marino Ballena entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition","wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"National Park wildlife walk (sloths + 4 monkey species)","status":"future","hook":"2- & 3-toed sloths, capuchins, endangered squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans — reliably seen with a certified scope-guide.","bookable_category":"guided park wildlife tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.adventuretourscostarica.com/blog/spotting-sloths-monkeys-your-manuel-antonio-wildlife-guide + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","blurb":"2- & 3-toed sloths, capuchins, endangered squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans — reliably seen with a certified scope-guide.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate or host-IATA guide; park entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Manuel Antonio National Park open on Tuesday?","a":"No — the park is closed every Tuesday, year-round including holidays. It is open Wednesday–Monday 07:00–16:00; adult entry is $18, children 2–12 $5, under-2 free, and advance online ticket purchase with your passport number is required — route the park visit Wed–Mon.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"Can you see whales near Manuel Antonio?","a":"Yes — nearby Marino Ballena / Uvita has two humpback seasons. Southern-Hemisphere humpbacks run Jul–Oct/Nov (peak Aug–Sep) and Northern-Hemisphere humpbacks Dec–Mar/Apr (peak Jan–Feb), a rare draw spanning both the green and dry seasons, ~45–60 min south by guided boat tour.","source":"puravidamoms.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"Is Manuel Antonio good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — it''s one of Costa Rica''s premier romance hubs. The cliffside-resort belt above the beach, led by adults-only Makanda by the Sea ~100 m above the ocean, defines the honeymoon identity, while Arenas del Mar is the only true beachfront luxury resort with two private beaches.","source":"oyster.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"Can you really see sloths and monkeys at the beach?","a":"Yes — it''s one of very few places anywhere you reliably can. Two- and three-toed sloths, white-faced capuchins (on 90%+ of visits), the endangered Central American squirrel monkey, howlers, coatis and toucans all live inside a compact, walkable national park where the rainforest meets the sand.","source":"adventuretourscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife-—-future","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"What''s the biggest safety risk in Manuel Antonio?","a":"Pacific rip currents — the leading cause of tourist drowning in Costa Rica (over 80% of drownings), on mostly unguarded beaches. Swim only at guarded/flagged beaches — the guarded park cove of Playa Manuel Antonio is the calmest water and the only patrolled swim — heed red flags, never swim alone, and if caught, swim parallel to shore.","source":"crie.cr, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"Are the monkeys a problem in the park?","a":"They can be — capuchins, raccoons and coatis are bold and habituated and will raid open bags and grab food. Don''t feed wildlife, keep food sealed and bags zipped, and don''t leave belongings unattended on the beach.","source":"adventuretourscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica Travel Guide — Sloths, Rainforest Beaches, Cliffside Resorts & Quepos | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"See sloths and monkeys at a Pacific beach, base on the Quepos cliffs for romance or in a villa for family, and do Manuel Antonio well, safely, and at the right time — park hours, riptide safety, whales, catamarans and waterfalls.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","local_keywords":["Parque Nacional Manuel Antonio","playas Manuel Antonio","qué hacer en Quepos","avistamiento de ballenas Uvita Marino Ballena","cataratas Nauyaca desde Manuel Antonio","kayak manglares isla Damas","perezosos y monos Manuel Antonio","hoteles de lujo Manuel Antonio","vuelo San José a Quepos","horario Parque Nacional Manuel Antonio precio entrada"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-06","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:18Z","source_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00"}]},"long_tail":["Manuel Antonio National Park hours 2026","is Manuel Antonio open on Tuesday","best time to visit Manuel Antonio Costa Rica","Manuel Antonio sloths and monkeys guide","Manuel Antonio riptide beach safety","SJO to Quepos flight Manuel Antonio","Manuel Antonio cliffside honeymoon resorts","Manuel Antonio villas with pool family","Nauyaca Waterfalls day trip from Manuel Antonio","Uvita whale watching season from Manuel Antonio"]},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Arenas del Mar (Böÿ Collection / Cayuga)","why_ultra":"The only true beachfront luxury resort in Manuel Antonio — private ridge, two secluded beaches (golf-cart access), rainforest all around, strong sustainability, ocean-view suites with plunge pools. The apex property.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + amenity block; agent-of-record commission","consortia_value_add":"upgrade, breakfast/resort credit, early/late, VIP welcome (confirm current program)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA agent-of-record","tier":"luxury / ultra"},{"name":"Makanda by the Sea","why_ultra":"Adults-only (16+), ~100 m above the ocean on 12 acres of rainforest gardens — the definitive Manuel Antonio honeymoon/romance property; small, private, view-forward.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + amenity","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit where program allows (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Gaia Hotel & Reserve","why_ultra":"Eco-chic adults-oriented 22-room private-reserve hillside hotel; 500-thread-count linens, wellness + service focus.","earning":"consortia/agent rate","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA","tier":"premier / luxury"},{"name":"Tulemar Resort (+ private villas)","why_ultra":"Gated hillside estate with its own private sandy beach, 4 pools, concierge, spa, and a portfolio of private villas — the best resort-serviced villa play for families/multi-gen.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + villa MoR","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit + villa perks (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA agent-of-record + villa direct-contract","tier":"premier / luxury (villas: luxury/ultra)"},{"name":"Preferred / luxury hillside villas","why_ultra":"Private ocean-view villas (chef/staff, pools, 2–8 br) — the whole-property-buyout ultra lane for honeymooners + multi-gen groups.","earning":"villa MoR + agent-of-record","consortia_value_add":"n/a (villa direct-contract perks vary)","mor":"direct-contract / villa specialist (host-IATA)","tier":"luxury / ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":9.392,"lng":-84.137},"orbit":[{"id":"guanacaste-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["tropical","expedition","liveaboard","wellness","wildlife"]},{"id":"la-fortuna-arenal-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["expedition","romance","wellness"]},{"id":"monteverde-costa-rica","jewels":12,"si":["expedition","wildlife","romance"]},{"id":"nosara-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["tropical","expedition","wellness"]},{"id":"osa-peninsula-corcovado-costa-rica","jewels":9,"si":["expedition","diveglobal"]},{"id":"puerto-viejo-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["tropical","expedition","culture","wildlife","ocean"]},{"id":"san-jose-costa-rica","jewels":13,"si":["culture","expedition"]},{"id":"tortuguero-costa-rica","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","river"]}],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 65)
