ril  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","si":"expedition","blurb":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%","wells":["activities","gear"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Uspallata & the high desert","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.myguideargentina.com/experiences/mendoza-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-day-trip","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","si":"expedition","blurb":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC day 10–20%","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Mendoza the world''s Malbec capital?","a":"Because the concentration is unmatched: Argentina holds roughly 75% of the world''s Malbec vines, and about 75% of Argentina''s vineyards lie in Mendoza — making it the single most important place on the planet for the grape and the global epicenter of Malbec.","source":"winefolly.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Mendoza?","a":"Late February through April — harvest and the Fiesta Nacional de la Vendimia (2026 central acts Mar 6–10) — is the most atmospheric window. Spring (Oct–Nov) is the value-and-balance alternative, with rates running ~15–25% below harvest peaks; either way, book icon wineries and lodges 3–4 months ahead of the Feb–April peak.","source":"across-southamerica.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"Which honeymoon wine-lodge should we book?","a":"The two ultra beds are Awasi Mendoza (Relais & Châteaux, Luján de Cuyo, 18 adobe rooms/villas on a ~60-acre private vineyard) and The Vines Resort & Spa (Valle de Uco, 21 private villas across 1,500 acres with vine-side dining). Both commission best through luxury consortia (Virtuoso/Fora), typically ~10%+ plus amenities.","source":"scottdunn.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"Can you see Aconcagua on a day trip from Mendoza?","a":"Yes. Route 7 climbs the Alta Montaña corridor past Potrerillos (1,350 m), Uspallata (1,900 m), and Puente del Inca (2,720 m) to the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak, the highest in the Western Hemisphere. The day-trip tops out ~2,700 m (mild breathlessness possible); Aconcagua summit mountaineering is a separate, expedition-grade activity requiring permits and licensed guides.","source":"getyourguide.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Mendoza?","a":"Drink-driving. Wine touring plus self-drive is the single most important avoidable risk, so the standard doctrine is always a designated driver or a guided wine tour with transport — never self-drive between tastings, and ride sober on the Maipú bike-and-wine route.","source":"machupicchu.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"Is Mendoza River rafting dangerous?","a":"Guided, it is a managed risk. Rafting at Potrerillos runs Class II–III, up to Class IV in high summer flow, with certified rescue guides, kayak safety support, and full neoprene/helmet/PFD standard — book certified operators only, and never run the river unguided.","source":"solsalute.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mendoza & Argentina Wine Country — Malbec, Valle de Uco & the Andes | TravelWell","search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["bodegas Mendoza","Valle de Uco vinos","Ruta del Vino Mendoza","Vendimia","Alta Montaña Aconcagua","termas de Cacheuta","Malbec de altura"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/argentina","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:24Z","source_updated":"2026-05-07T17:26:11+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Awasi Mendoza (formerly Cavas Wine Lodge)","brand":"Relais & Châteaux","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"18 adobe rooms/villas on ~60-acre private vineyard","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"The Vines Resort & Spa","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"21 private vineyard villas on 1,500 acres + spa + vine-side dining","earning":"consortia commission + villa MoR","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa de Uco","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"modern estate rooms, pool + spa, working-vineyard finca","earning":"consortia / DMC commission","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Entre Cielos","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"design hotel in 3.2 ha Malbec vines + Hammam spa circuit","earning":"consortia / bedbank premium","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Mendoza & the Wine Country, Argentina, Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-32.8895,"lng":-68.8458},"orbit":[{"id":"iguazu-falls-argentina","jewels":10,"si":["expedition","culture"]},{"id":"salta-argentina","jewels":10,"si":["culture","expedition","culinary","romance"]}],"orbit_country":["buenos-aires-argentina","el-calafate-argentina","peninsula-valdes-argentina"]}'::jsonb, 68),
  ('merida-mexico', '10S', 'Mérida, Yucatán', 'Mexico', 'Mérida Yucatán travel guide', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"culinary","culture","expedition","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Capital of Yucatán state and the peninsula''s cultural + medical hub; nicknamed ''La Ciudad Blanca'' (the White City).","The FCDO names no advisory against travel to Yucatán.","Heart of the restored-hacienda hotel circuit — Chablé, four Luxury Collection haciendas, Angsana Xcanatún — the region''s signature luxury supply.","Distinct Yucatecan cuisine (cochinita pibil, sopa de lima, mucbipollo) centered on the 1887 Mercado Lucas de Gálvez (~2,000 stalls).","Gateway to cenote country, Celestún/Río Lagartos flamingos, Uxmal + Ruta Puuc, and Chichén Itzá; Gulf beach at Progreso ~35 min north."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Star Médica Mérida; Christus Muguerza Faro del Mayab; Centro Médico de las Américas (CMA); Clínica de Mérida — regional trauma/medical hub","air_access_verified":"MID — Mérida Manuel Crescencio Rejón International (direct US: DFW, IAH, MIA)","heat":"Hot-humid May–Sep; Apr–Jun can exceed 100°F (38°C) — extreme-heat protocol on daytime ruin/cenote outings","water":"Bottled only (do not drink tap; use bottled for tooth-brushing)","malaria":"No malaria risk in Mérida / Yucatán tourist corridor; dengue present, chikungunya rising (2025–26) — mosquito precautions","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-09-04T12:02:56Z","page_updated":"2026-09-04T00:25:51+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"~2026-10-25 (Hanal Pixán opening; late-Oct heat break + end of hurricane season lifts demand off baseline)","peak":"December–April (tightest Dec–March; dry-cool, low humidity)","fire_date":"2026-10-10","shoulder":"November; late April–early May","green":"May–September (hot-humid; Apr–Jun can exceed 100°F/38°C; rains peak Jun–Sep)","booking_lead":"Hacienda weddings 6–12 months (advised 10–12); leisure 1–3 months, longer for Hanal Pixán week","off_season_specials":"Summer hacienda + mansion-boutique rate softening; cenote-and-spa ''White City in the Green Season'' packaging; indoor culture year-round","event_peaks":["Hanal Pixán / Festival de las Ánimas (Oct 25–Nov 2)","Mérida Fest (early-mid January; 2026 ran Jan 5–18)","Flamingo season Nov–Feb (Celestún / Río Lagartos)"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Paseo de Montejo mansions (Casa Museo Montes Molina)","status":"future","hook":"The gilded-age face of Yucatán''s ''green gold''","bookable_category":"guided walking tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.kupi.com/en-ae/explore/mexico/merida/paseo-de-montejo","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The gilded-age face of Yucatán''s ''green gold''","when":"December–April","commission":"Viator/local guide affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Gran Museo del Mundo Maya","status":"future","hook":"The intellectual on-ramp before your first ruin","bookable_category":"entry + guided combo","tier":"essential","source":"https://travel.usnews.com/Merida_Mexico/Things_To_Do/El_Gran_Museo_del_Mundo_Maya_de_Mrida_65503/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The intellectual on-ramp before your first ruin","when":"December–April","commission":"affiliate (entry non-commissionable)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Izamal — The Yellow Town + Convento de San Antonio","status":"future","hook":"The most photogenic town in Yucatán","bookable_category":"private day-trip + transfer","tier":"comfort","s