v 2","commission":"private artisan-village tour (DMC); rug purchases direct-to-artisan","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"San Bartolo Coyotepec black pottery","tier":"essential","source":"https://theculturetrip.com/north-america/mexico/articles/a-tour-of-oaxacas-best-markets","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"south-valley artisan tour (DMC)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Alebrijes at San Martin Tilcajete","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.fiestamericanatravelty.com/en/grand-fiesta-americana/hotels/grand-fiesta-americana-oaxaca","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"artisan-workshop tour + hotel alebrije programming","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Terrain and high-proof spirits, not crime. The city is a mild **~1,555 m** (light first-day breathlessness at most); the genuine hazards are Hierve el Agua''s cliff-edge footing above a canyon and the mezcal route — high-proof tastings plus rural highway driving mean you take a driver or DMC, never self-drive after tasting.","source":"oaxacalife.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"q":"When is Día de Muertos, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"Oct 31–Nov 2, and it''s the longest lead time in the inland catalog: book **4–8 months ahead** (5–6 months / May–June is the sweet spot). Walkable-Centro rooms are ~95% booked by early September and rates run **2–3× normal** ($150–250 USD/night).","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com / wheregoesrose.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culture","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"q":"Is Oaxaca really a top food destination?","a":"Yes — it''s widely regarded as one of the world''s great food capitals. The \"seven moles,\" market-to-table cooking schools (Casa Crespo), and the mezcal terroir of Santiago Matatlán (~45 minutes southeast, the World Capital of Mezcal) are destination-defining reasons to go.","source":"oaxaca-mio.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culinary","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"q":"Is Hierve el Agua worth it — and will it be open?","a":"Worth it, but verify first. The petrified mineral \"waterfalls\" and clifftop spring-fed pools sit 70 km east near Mitla, but the site sees **periodic community-dispute closures clustering June–October** — always confirm it''s open the week before, and keep a Mitla + Tlacolula fallback ready.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"expedition","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"q":"Is Oaxaca good for couples?","a":"Yes — a slow, sensory, non-beach romance. Boutique casonas and the ex-convent (1576) Quinta Real, mezcal-tasting date nights, and the artisan-village shopping ritual (Teotitlán weaving, rugs $75–$500; San Bartolo black pottery; alebrijes) make the case.","source":"caminoreal.com / brokenbootstravel.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"romance","accessed":"2026-07-05"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Oaxaca City & the Central Valleys, Mexico — UNESCO, Mezcal, Dia de Muertos & Monte Alban | TravelWell.World","search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Dia de Muertos Oaxaca","que hacer en Oaxaca","ruta del mezcal","Guelaguetza fechas","Monte Alban precio entrada","Hierve el Agua abierto","hoteles boutique Oaxaca centro","Noche de Rabanos"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-05","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-05","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["romance","expedition"],"ultra":[{"name":"Quinta Real Oaxaca","positioning":"ex-Convent of Santa Catalina (1576), 91 rooms, UNESCO Centre","earning_path":"consortia/Virtuoso + Fora lane","mor":"hotel","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Escondido Oaxaca","positioning":"Grupo Habita design-boutique, rooftop pool","earning_path":"Grupo Habita direct + consortia/Fora","mor":"hotel","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Pug Seal Oaxaca","positioning":"top-cited Centro design-boutique","earning_path":"consortia/Fora","mor":"hotel","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Hotel Sin Nombre","positioning":"intimate quiet-luxury design hotel","earning_path":"Fora/direct","mor":"hotel","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa Antonieta","positioning":"9-room boutique casona, affordable-ultra entry","earning_path":"OTA + boutique-collection/Fora","mor":"hotel","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-05","hero":{"query":"Oaxaca City & the Central Valleys, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":